<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carl XVI Gustaf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1946</span> · Also known as Carl XVI Gustaf of Sweden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carl XVI Gustaf has been King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> since 15 September 1973, succeeding his grandfather Gustaf VI Adolf. The Instrument of Government of 1974 left him a purely ceremonial head of state without political powers, and a change in the law in 1980 made his elder daughter, Crown Princess Victoria, heir to the throne. He is the longest-reigning monarch in Swedish history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carl-xvi-gustaf.jpg" alt="Carl XVI Gustaf" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lula Oficial · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:06.11.2025_%E2%80%93_Recep%C3%A7%C3%A3o_Oficial_dos_Chefes_de_Delega%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_C%C3%BApula_do_Clima_(54906269035)_(Carlos_XVI_Gustavo).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
